@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Keep the typed text when leaving a thread
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}

actor "Member" as actor
box "Frontend — Popkin web app" #E0F2FE
  participant "GroupChatPage\n(pk-composer)" as page
  participant "DraftStore" as drafts
  participant "Router" as router
end box
actor -> page : Type text without sending
page -> drafts : set(threadId, text) on each change
actor -> router : Navigate away (Back, nav tab)
router -> page : The page is destroyed; the draft is already saved
actor -> router : Return to the thread in the same session
router -> page : The page opens; once the thread is read
page -> drafts : get(threadId)
drafts --> page : Saved text
page --> actor : Message field holds the text (L2-028 AC4)
opt message sent
  page -> drafts : set(threadId, ""), which removes the draft
end
note over drafts : Drafts and the outbox are not cleared at sign-out yet:\nthat arrives with sign out (journey 17).
@enduml
